{"arxivId": "1909.11942", "groupId": "abstract-paper-1909.11942", "sourceURL": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.11942", "split": "dev", "sampleId": "sample-89be18fceeb4a62533d0", "sourceSampleId": "sample-74a2479c98c58d01f722", "sourceTextSha256": "3b8a398fd2c0681e9337412e4db33d59ef5975f07d5ae0d7fe74ccbadebc9f34", "sourceStart": 529, "sourceEnd": 855, "block": 3, "textKind": "abstract_evidence_block", "text": "We also use a self-supervised loss that focuses on modeling inter-sentence coherence, and show it consistently helps downstream tasks with multi-sentence inputs. As a result, our best model establishes new state-of-the-art results on the GLUE, RACE, and \\squad benchmarks while having fewer parameters compared to BERT-large. ", "textSha256": "e90b8a7ab3bcf4c71479f849ca3e056b31ddbf12a5d033150ce5b115e5f54466", "entities": [{"entityId": "e1", "start": 14, "end": 34, "text": "self-supervised loss", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e2", "start": 51, "end": 84, "text": "modeling inter-sentence coherence", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e3", "start": 238, "end": 242, "text": "GLUE", "label": "DATASET"}, {"entityId": "e4", "start": 244, "end": 248, "text": "RACE", "label": "DATASET"}, {"entityId": "e5", "start": 254, "end": 260, "text": "\\squad", "label": "DATASET"}, {"entityId": "e6", "start": 314, "end": 324, "text": "BERT-large", "label": "METHOD"}], "entityStatus": "complete", "entityReason": "", "reason": "At least one local pair remains UNRESOLVED"}
{"arxivId": "2006.03654", "groupId": "abstract-paper-2006.03654", "sourceURL": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.03654", "split": "dev", "sampleId": "sample-874e4a5b8aa027e07952", "sourceSampleId": "sample-fa2a676d1b0eea9d662e", "sourceTextSha256": "6e51be908ca93534b364ac20ace62314008e7b4062020faa0f94c542e346ca3b", "sourceStart": 763, "sourceEnd": 1087, "block": 3, "textKind": "abstract_evidence_block", "text": "In addition, a new virtual adversarial training method is used for fine-tuning to improve models' generalization. We show that these techniques significantly improve the efficiency of model pre-training and the performance of both natural language understanding (NLU) and natural langauge generation (NLG) downstream tasks. ", "textSha256": "b8696c5d2a3f4764c929af2f9335598c35593ba463bb5d0da4f450f47e52b835", "entities": [{"entityId": "e1", "start": 19, "end": 47, "text": "virtual adversarial training", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e2", "start": 184, "end": 202, "text": "model pre-training", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e3", "start": 231, "end": 261, "text": "natural language understanding", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e4", "start": 263, "end": 266, "text": "NLU", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e5", "start": 272, "end": 299, "text": "natural langauge generation", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e6", "start": 301, "end": 304, "text": "NLG", "label": "TASK"}], "entityStatus": "complete", "entityReason": "", "reason": "At least one local pair remains UNRESOLVED"}
{"arxivId": "1908.10084", "groupId": "abstract-paper-1908.10084", "sourceURL": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.10084", "split": "dev", "sampleId": "sample-e0844ac2f726c3c3f1ad", "sourceSampleId": "sample-d972dc374490084c3c52", "sourceTextSha256": "0c1c8ed261f75c76beed4bda3912d293019349c6808e27aafbade2829bfd0065", "sourceStart": 0, "sourceEnd": 427, "block": 1, "textKind": "abstract_evidence_block", "text": "BERT (Devlin et al., 2018) and RoBERTa (Liu et al., 2019) has set a new state-of-the-art performance on sentence-pair regression tasks like semantic textual similarity (STS). However, it requires that both sentences are fed into the network, which causes a massive computational overhead: Finding the most similar pair in a collection of 10,000 sentences requires about 50 million inference computations (~65 hours) with BERT. ", "textSha256": "251dbb94ee55847eb5408b6685c75a18598eb7c4489f52c5e7ad239b74f95670", "entities": [{"entityId": "e1", "start": 0, "end": 4, "text": "BERT", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e2", "start": 31, "end": 38, "text": "RoBERTa", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e3", "start": 104, "end": 128, "text": "sentence-pair regression", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e4", "start": 140, "end": 167, "text": "semantic textual similarity", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e5", "start": 169, "end": 172, "text": "STS", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e6", "start": 289, "end": 318, "text": "Finding the most similar pair", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e7", "start": 421, "end": 425, "text": "BERT", "label": "METHOD"}], "entityStatus": "complete", "entityReason": "", "reason": "At least one local pair remains UNRESOLVED"}
{"arxivId": "1908.10084", "groupId": "abstract-paper-1908.10084", "sourceURL": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.10084", "split": "dev", "sampleId": "sample-c93e1647f8da1de5feea", "sourceSampleId": "sample-d972dc374490084c3c52", "sourceTextSha256": "0c1c8ed261f75c76beed4bda3912d293019349c6808e27aafbade2829bfd0065", "sourceStart": 427, "sourceEnd": 803, "block": 2, "textKind": "abstract_evidence_block", "text": "The construction of BERT makes it unsuitable for semantic similarity search as well as for unsupervised tasks like clustering. In this publication, we present Sentence-BERT (SBERT), a modification of the pretrained BERT network that use siamese and triplet network structures to derive semantically meaningful sentence embeddings that can be compared using cosine-similarity. ", "textSha256": "69e05069526d845cb89279fb2b640776c38f472d8181df081affb1d15056cab8", "entities": [{"entityId": "e1", "start": 20, "end": 24, "text": "BERT", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e2", "start": 49, "end": 75, "text": "semantic similarity search", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e3", "start": 115, "end": 125, "text": "clustering", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e4", "start": 159, "end": 172, "text": "Sentence-BERT", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e5", "start": 174, "end": 179, "text": "SBERT", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e6", "start": 215, "end": 219, "text": "BERT", "label": "METHOD"}, {"entityId": "e7", "start": 279, "end": 329, "text": "derive semantically meaningful sentence embeddings", "label": "TASK"}, {"entityId": "e8", "start": 357, "end": 374, "text": "cosine-similarity", "label": "METHOD"}], "entityStatus": "unresolved", "entityReason": "Shared-head group cannot become complete flat BIO entities", "reason": "Shared-head group cannot become complete flat BIO entities"}
